2 provisional sets - 1 successful union = 1 final component. 5 foreground cells; 4 union attempts; 13 find calls.
\image(figures/component_bridge.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The bottom-right cell makes the bridge. The first scan leaves the original top-right provisional ID 2 in place; the second scan changes it to dense component ID 1. Rows increase downwards and all zero cells are background.)
\alttext(Two native two-row grids show provisional labels 1,0,2 above 1,1,1 on the left, and final labels 1,0,1 above 1,1,1 on the right.)

Why is this correct? After each scanned foreground cell, the union-find sets
represent the components of the foreground graph induced by the visited cells.
A cell with no earlier neighbour starts a new component. Otherwise adding it
joins exactly the earlier components incident to its edges. Every undirected
edge is considered once, when its later endpoint is scanned. Induction therefore
accounts for every permitted edge, including paths that merge old provisional
sets much later. The second pass changes names rather than membership, so equal
positive output IDs are equivalent to foreground connectivity.

The forest now uses union by rank with path halving. On equal rank, the smaller
root ID wins; otherwise higher rank wins even if its ID is larger. A rank increase
requires combining two equally ranked trees, so a rank-r root represents at least
2^r provisional sets. This bounds ranks and prevents arbitrary linear-depth
attachments. Rank plus halving gives the amortised inverse-Ackermann bound.
The former implementation used halving with unbalanced unions; the stated bound
was not justified by those heuristics alone.

> Diagonal contact changes the objects

A three-by-three checkerboard contains five foreground cells. With four-neighbour
adjacency they are five singletons. With eight-neighbour adjacency they form one
component through the centre. Connectivity is a modelling choice, not a cosmetic
renaming of an unchanged partition.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/component_connectivity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto image=dm::algorithms::component_checkerboard(3,3);
  const auto four=dm::algorithms::connected_components(image);
  const auto eight=dm::algorithms::connected_components(image,true);
  dm::graphics::diagram_label_images({{four.labels,"Four neighbours: five IDs"},
    {eight.labels,"Eight neighbours: one ID"}}).save_svg("build/component_connectivity.svg");
  std::print("| connectivity | components | component | area | grid perimeter | centroid row | centroid col |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& [name,result]:std::array<std::pair<std::string_view,dm::algorithms::ConnectedComponents>,2>{{{"four",four},{"eight",eight}}})
    for(const auto& s:dm::algorithms::connected_component_stats(result))
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |\n",name,result.count,s.label,s.area,s.perimeter4,s.centroid_row,s.centroid_col);
}
```
