| connectivity | components | component | area | grid perimeter | centroid row | centroid col |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| four | 5 | 1 | 1 | 4 | 0.000 | 0.000 |
| four | 5 | 2 | 1 | 4 | 0.000 | 2.000 |
| four | 5 | 3 | 1 | 4 | 1.000 | 1.000 |
| four | 5 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2.000 | 0.000 |
| four | 5 | 5 | 1 | 4 | 2.000 | 2.000 |
| eight | 1 | 1 | 5 | 20 | 1.000 | 1.000 |
\image(figures/component_connectivity.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Diagonal adjacency merges the five checkerboard cells into one region. Its exposed orthogonal edge count remains twenty: diagonal contact shares no orthogonal edge.)
\alttext(Two three-by-three grids have the same five occupied checkerboard cells. The left uses five positive IDs and colours; the right uses ID one at every occupied cell.)

The reported perimeter is a discrete measurement: each exposed orthogonal unit
cell edge contributes one, even when eight-connectivity created the component.
For area A and E same-label orthogonal adjacent pairs,

\[
P_4=4A-2E.
\]
\alttext(The grid perimeter is four times cell count minus twice the number of same-label orthogonally adjacent pairs.)

Each shared edge removes two of the four per-cell edges. Holes contribute their
inner exposed edges. This count is not a smooth Euclidean perimeter estimator;
changing diagonal connectivity need not change its total for a fixed mask.
The centroid is the mean of zero-based cell-centre row and column indices, and
bounds include their minimum and maximum indices.

> Original example: four separate rectangles

The original twelve-by-twelve mask is now a deterministic native fixture. Its
inclusive rectangle bounds are (1,1)-(3,3), (1,7)-(2,10), (6,2)-(9,3) and
(7,7)-(10,10), written as (row,column). It contains 41 foreground cells and 103
background cells. Both connectivity choices leave four regions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/connected_components.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto image=dm::algorithms::component_blobs_example();
  const auto a=dm::algorithms::connected_components_analyze(image);
  const auto eight=dm::algorithms::connected_components(image,true);
  dm::graphics::diagram_label_images({{a.result.labels,"Original four rectangles"}})
    .save_svg("build/connected_components.svg");
  std::print("| ID | area | inclusive rows | inclusive columns | centroid (row,col) | exposed grid edges |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: |\n");
  std::size_t area=0;
  for(const auto& s:dm::algorithms::connected_component_stats(a.result)) {
    std::print("| {} | {} | [{},{}] | [{},{}] | ({:.1f},{:.1f}) | {} |\n",s.label,s.area,s.min_row,s.max_row,s.min_col,s.max_col,s.centroid_row,s.centroid_col,s.perimeter4);
    area+=s.area;
  }
  const auto& w=a.work;
  std::print("\nComponents: {}; eight-neighbour count: {}; equal label maps: {}. Foreground area: {}.\n",a.result.count,eight.count,a.result.labels==eight.labels,area);
  std::print("Provisional sets: {}; successful unions: {}; all union attempts: {}; find calls: {}.\n",w.labels_created,w.successful_unions,w.union_calls,w.find_calls);
}
```
